    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45407" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐφημ-ισμός</span></b> , ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>use of an auspicious word
				for an inauspicious one</i>, e.g. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὐμενίδες</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐρινύες,
				εὐφρόνη</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύξ</span>,
			etc., <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1398.52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				281
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ εὐφημισμόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Corn.
					<u>ND</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Prog.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Palaeph.
				51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Olymp.
				<u>in Mete.</u>
				105.19
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ᾽ εὐφημισμοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Piet.</u>
					111
				</span></i>
			.</div>
